          "0": {
            "id": "14047643",
            "headline": "HD Fire Protect IPO GMP at 30% ahead of October 13 issue opening; check lot size, timeline and key details here",
            "heading": "HD Fire Protect IPO GMP at 30% ahead of October 13 issue opening; check lot size, timeline and key details here",
            "intro": "HD Fire Protect IPO is commanding a grey market premium (GMP) of around 30% ahead of its subscription opening on October 13, according to market tracking platform InvestorGain.",
            "body": "HD Fire Protect IPO is commanding a grey market premium (GMP) of around 30 percent ahead of its subscription opening on October 13, according to market tracking platform InvestorGain.\r\n\r\nHD Fire Protect has fixed the price band for its Rs 712.31 crore initial public offering (IPO) at Rs 258-271 per equity share. The issue will open for subscription on October 13 and close on October 15, 2026.\r\n\r\nRead Also:\u00a0Left TCS job, built Rs 20-crore 'ThickShake Factory': How Yeshwanth Nag turned a milkshake idea into a business\r\n\r\nAt a GMP of 29.52 percent, the unlisted market is currently indicating a potential listing price of around Rs 351 per share against the upper end of the IPO price band of Rs 271. This translates into a potential listing gain of around Rs 80 per share, although grey market premiums are unofficial and can change before listing.\r\n\r\nGMP is an unofficial indicator of market sentiment and is not a guaranteed indication of the actual listing price.\r\n\r\nThe IPO is entirely an offer for sale (OFS) of 2,62,84,500 equity shares worth Rs 712.31 crore. Since the issue comprises only an OFS, HD Fire Protect will not receive any proceeds from the IPO. The entire amount raised will go to the selling shareholders.\r\n\r\nPromoter Harish Narshi Dharamshi will sell 89,83,700 shares worth Rs 243.46 crore, while promoter Kusum Harish Dharamshi will offload 1,73,00,800 shares worth Rs 468.85 crore.\r\n\r\nTogether, the two promoter shareholders are selling 2.63 crore shares, aggregating Rs 712.31 crore.\r\n\r\nThe allotment of shares is expected to be finalised on October 16, while the shares are proposed to be listed on both the NSE and BSE on October 21.\r\n\r\nThe IPO has a lot size of 55 shares. At the upper end of the price band, retail investors will need to invest a minimum of Rs 14,905 to subscribe to one lot.\r\n\r\n&amp;nbsp;\r\n\r\nCheck IPO News Here\r\n\r\nHD Fire Protect reported a 12 percent year-on-year increase in total income to Rs 505 crore in Fiscal 2026 from Rs 451 crore in Fiscal 2025.\r\n\r\nIts profit after tax (PAT) increased 6\u00a0percent to Rs 117 crore in Fiscal 2026, compared with Rs 110 crore in the previous fiscal.\r\n\r\nRevenue from operations rose from Rs 372.95 crore in Fiscal 2024 to Rs 489.28 crore in Fiscal 2026, representing a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 14.54 percent.\r\n\r\nAbout HD Fire Protect\r\n\r\nIncorporated in April 1997, HD Fire Protect manufactures and supplies fire protection equipment and systems, including water-, foam- and gas-based fire suppression solutions.\r\n\r\nIts product portfolio covers eight categories, including sprinklers, alarm and deluge valves, foam equipment, monitors and nozzles, water spray nozzles, custom-engineered systems and gas suppression systems.\r\n\r\nThe company caters to industrial, residential and commercial customers across sectors such as oil and gas, petrochemicals, power, engineering, aerospace, pharmaceuticals, data centres, hospitality and healthcare.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: The views and investment tips expressed by investment experts on Moneycontrol.com are their own and not those of the website or its management. Moneycontrol.com advises users to check with certified experts before taking any investment decisions.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/hd-fire-protect-ipo-gmp-at-30-ahead-of-october-13-issue-opening-check-lot-size-timeline-and-key-details-here-14047643.html",
            "ai_impact_text_summary_s": "HD Fire Protect's Rs 712.31 crore IPO opens on October 13 with a price band of Rs 258-271 per share. The issue is an offer for sale, commanding a grey market premium of about 30%, with shares slated to list on NSE and BSE on October 21.",
