            "id": "14047513",
            "headline": "Avaada Electro said to plan $786 million India IPO in November",
            "heading": "Avaada Electro said to plan $786 million India IPO in November",
            "intro": "Avaada Electro confidentially filed draft documents in October 2025 to raise as much as Rs 7,600 crore ($786 million) and received regulatory approval in April",
            "body": "Avaada Electro Ltd., the solar manufacturing arm of Avaada Group, is planning to launch an initial public offering as early as next month, according to people familiar with the matter.\r\n\r\nThe Brookfield Renewable Partners-backed company is meeting potential investors and is targeting a launch around mid-November, the people said, asking not to be identified because the information is private.\r\n\r\nAvaada Electro confidentially filed draft documents in October 2025 to raise as much as Rs 7,600 crore ($786 million) and received regulatory approval in April. The IPO comprises a fresh issue of shares worth up to Rs 1,600 crore and an offer for sale of up to Rs 6,000 crore by parent Avaada Ventures Pvt., according to the filing.\r\n\r\nICICI Securities Ltd., Axis Capital Ltd., Bank of America Corp., HSBC Holdings Plc, SBI Capital Markets Ltd. and IIFL Capital Services Ltd. are helping manage the potential share sale, the filing showed.\r\n\r\nDeliberations are ongoing and details including the timing and size of the offering could change, the people said. A representative for Avaada Group didn\u2019t respond to requests for comment.\r\n\r\nProceeds from IPOs in India reached almost $10 billion in July-September, thanks to blockbuster offerings by National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. and SBI Funds Management Ltd. The country is now on track for one of its best years ever, with nearly $14 billion raised already by 278 IPOs, data compiled by Bloomberg show.\r\n\r\nAvaada Electro makes high-efficiency solar photovoltaic cells and modules, according to its website. It operates 8.5 gigawatts of solar-module manufacturing capacity across Nagpur and Dadri and plans to add another 5.1 gigawatts, taking total capacity to 13.6 gigawatts.",
