            "headline": "Sollfege Smart Electronics SME shares hit 5% lower circuit post 90% listing gains",
            "heading": "Sollfege Smart Electronics SME shares hit 5% lower circuit post 90% listing gains",
            "intro": "Shares of the company made a strong market debut, listing at Rs 104.40, a premium of 89.81% over the issue price.",
            "body": "Sollfege Smart Electronics SME shares hit the 5 percent lower circuit on Thursday amid profit booking at higher levels, shortly after the company made a strong market debut with an almost 90 percent premium.\r\n\r\nShares of the company were quoted at Rs 99.18 per share on the BSE, down 5 percent, its lowest permissible trading limit for the session.\r\n\r\nEarlier in the day, the shares made a strong market debut, listing at Rs 104.40, a premium of 89.81 percent over the issue price.\r\n\r\nKolkata-based Sollfege Smart Electronics, which provides audio, video, home automation and smart living solutions, had raised Rs 21.78 crore through an initial share sale of 39.6 lakh shares at a fixed price of Rs 55 apiece.\r\n\r\nThe IPO was subscribed 2.08 times during the three-day bidding period, with investors placing bids for 82.56 lakh shares through 995 applications.\r\n\r\nThe company will use the net issue proceeds to expand its retail network by launching 12 new showrooms, meet working capital requirements and fund general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: The views and investment tips expressed by investment experts on Moneycontrol.com are their own and not those of the website or its management. Moneycontrol.com advises users to check with certified experts before taking any investment decisions.",
